			"Message": "docs(Sky): Update InstallTests JSDoc now that ITestService is exposed\n\n`Source/Function/Sky/Bridge/InstallTests.ts` previously documented that `ITestService` was absent from `globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__`. The workbench accessor plugin now exposes `TestService` via `Output/Source/Service/CEL/Expose/Accessor.ts`, so the module-level doc comment is updated to reflect the current state and clarify that services are invoked directly when available.\n\nAlso normalizes an em-dash to an en-dash in the service-missing log message for consistency with surrounding convention.",
			"SHA": "42318a959d1fefdbe269b9aed5470ead692b7661"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T23:17:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				157,
				9
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Bridge test-runner channels and respect webview extension options\n\nAdd `Bridge/InstallTests.ts` to receive `sky://tests/*` events from Mountain/Cocoon — controller creation, run start/end, and per-item test results. Routes data to `cel:tests:*` DOM CustomEvents and probes `__CEL_SERVICES__?.TestService` for forward-compatible native Testing panel integration, logging a one-shot gap message when the service is absent.\n\nUpdate `InstallWebview.ts` to read extension-provided `options` from `createWebviewPanel` payloads, overriding hardcoded defaults for `retainContextWhenHidden`, `enableFindWidget`, `enableScripts`, `enableForms`, and `localResourceRoots`. Extensions that opt out of context retention (e.g. lightweight stateless panels) are no longer forced into the keep-alive path.\n\nFormat documentation tables consistently with en-dash separators and aligned column widths across Architecture.md and both READMEs. No functional change in the documentation edits.",
			"SHA": "d7893913b5f69b09dea618c1cca1727b0a9376f2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:34:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				156,
				2
			],
			"Message": "docs(Sky): Document shim architecture and add element README\n\nAdd a \"Shim Compatibility\" section to the Architecture documentation covering Sky's role in the Land deep-shim interception system — the component receives events from Wind via bridge, with no shim-specific modules of its own. Covers both Low-Level (TierShim=Own|Preempt) and Coverage (TierShim=Proxy|Replace) tiers, noting zero overhead when TierShim is None.\n\nCreate a standalone README for the Sky repository that describes its role as the browser-side bridge layer managing the editor webview lifecycle, with a cross-reference to Architecture.md and the same shim compatibility table.",
			"SHA": "a796ea91b41eb16ffb907a25e92730d10dcefeb0"
